lctech F1C200s: wire spi1 to the DMA engine for the ESP-Hosted link

Board-side only. NDMA DRQ 0x05 = SPI1 Rx/Tx per the F1C200s User Manual
V1.2 sections 3.6.7.4 and 7.3.7.5. spi-sun6i needs no changes: it
requests the channels and enables its FIFO DRQ bits automatically,
turning the ESP-Hosted transfers from ~25 FIFO interrupts per 1600-byte
frame into DMA (motivation: wireless Android Auto streams the whole AV
feed over this link; see docs/wireless-esp-hosted.md P6). Without the
channels spi-sun6i falls back to PIO, so this is an optimisation, not a
requirement.

On 6.6 this patch also carried a backport of the whole A10-class
NDMA/DDMA driver plus the dtsi controller node. Both are upstream as of
6.18 -- drivers/dma/sun4i-dma.c has suniv_f1c100s_dma_cfg with the
f1c100s data-width/burst variants, drivers/dma/Kconfig already allows
MACH_SUNIV, and suniv-f1c100s.dtsi carries dma-controller@1c02000 plus
the dt-bindings include. Only the board wiring is left, since upstream
leaves spi1's dmas unset.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/suniv-f1c200s-lctech-pi.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/suniv-f1c200s-lctech-pi.dts
@@ -73,6 +73,11 @@
 &spi1 {
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&spi1_pe_pins>;
+	/* NDMA DRQ 0x05 = SPI1 Rx/Tx (F1C200s manual 3.6.7.4); spi-sun6i
+	 * uses the channels automatically and falls back to PIO without. */
+	dmas = <&dma SUN4I_DMA_NORMAL 5>,
+	       <&dma SUN4I_DMA_NORMAL 5>;
+	dma-names = "rx", "tx";
 	status = "okay";
 };
